  "explain": [
    "Run on the S&P 500 at one XSP contract (139% of a $55,000 sleeve), the overlay changed the 2018-2026 Sharpe from 0.75 to 0.60, volatility from 16.2% to 12.6% and the worst drawdown from -24% to -24%, after costs.",
    "Option prices are modelled from the VIX with a smile fitted to CBOE's BXMD index on 2010-2017 only; out of sample the like-for-like model tracks that index with an error of 2.0% a year.",
    "On the standalone test it fails method.md rule 8.5; the S&P 500 options hedge the international half of the sleeve only loosely (correlation 0.83)."
